{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "35ab663c-5737-41a7-b6d1-5e4704a48fa9",
    "name": "Blog Application REST API",
    "description": "Automated Postman collection for the Blog Application REST API (Express.js + Sequelize + MySQL).\n\n**Batch No: 19 | Topic: API Development**\n\n### How it works\n- All dynamic values (`firstname`, `lastname`, `email`, `password`, `token`, `userId`, `blogId`, ...) are stored as **collection variables** and are set automatically by the pre-request / test scripts of each request — you do not need to type them in manually.\n- `Register User` generates a brand-new random `firstname`, `lastname`, `email` and `password` every time it runs (using the current timestamp), so you can re-run the whole collection repeatedly (e.g. with Collection Runner or Newman) without hitting the `409 email already registered` conflict.\n- `Login User` automatically stores the returned JWT in `{{token}}`, which is then reused by every protected request via Bearer auth.\n- `Admin Login` uses the separate `adminEmail` / `adminPassword` collection variables. Before running it, promote a registered user to admin as described in the main project README:\n  ```sql\n  UPDATE users SET role = 'admin' WHERE email = 'admin@example.com';\n  ```\n\n### Run order\nRun folders top to bottom: **Auth → Admin Setup → Users → Blogs**. Requests inside each folder must also run in order because later requests depend on variables set by earlier ones (`userId`, `token`, `adminToken`, `blogId`).\n\n### Running with Newman (CLI automation)\n```bash\nnpm install -g newman\nnewman run BlogAPI.postman_collection.json -e BlogAPI.postman_environment.json\n```",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Global automation check applied to every request in the collection",
          "pm.test('Response time is acceptable (< 3000ms)', function () {",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(3000);",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5000/api", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "firstname", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "lastname", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "newPassword", "value": "NewPass123", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "role", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "blogId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminEmail", "value": "admin@example.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "admin123", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminToken", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 - Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Generate a unique user on every run so the collection can be re-executed repeatedly",
                  "const timestamp = Date.now();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('firstname', 'Test');",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('lastname', 'User' + timestamp);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('email', `testuser${timestamp}@example.com`);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('password', 'Pass' + timestamp);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has success message', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.message).to.eql('user registered successfully');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('User data returned without password', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('id');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('email', pm.collectionVariables.get('email'));",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', jsonData.data.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firstname\": \"{{firstname}}\",\n  \"lastname\": \"{{lastname}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Register a new user. `firstname`, `lastname`, `email` and `password` are generated dynamically by the pre-request script so this request can be re-run without a duplicate-email conflict."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Login successful and token received', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.message).to.eql('login successful');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', jsonData.token);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('role', jsonData.data.role);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Logs in with the `email` / `password` generated by the Register User request and stores the returned JWT in `{{token}}`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
